<article class="env-lemma" id="0397">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0397">Lemma <span data-tag="0397">29.30.5</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Assume $f$ is locally of finite type. Let $x \in X$ with $s = f(x)$. Then $f$ is quasi-finite at $x$ if and only if $\dim _ x(X_ s) = 0$. In particular, $f$ is locally quasi-finite if and only if $f$ has relative dimension $0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      First proof. If $f$ is quasi-finite at $x$ then $\kappa (x)$ is a finite extension of $\kappa (s)$ (by Lemma <a href="/tag/01TG" data-tag="01TG">29.21.5</a>) and $x$ is isolated in $X_ s$ (by Lemma <a href="/tag/01TH" data-tag="01TH">29.21.6</a>), hence $\dim _ x(X_ s) = 0$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/02FX" data-tag="02FX">29.29.1</a>. Conversely, if $\dim _ x(X_ s) = 0$ then by Lemma <a href="/tag/02FX" data-tag="02FX">29.29.1</a> we see $\kappa (s) \subset \kappa (x)$ is algebraic and there are no other points of $X_ s$ specializing to $x$. Hence $x$ is closed in its fibre by Lemma <a href="/tag/01TE" data-tag="01TE">29.21.2</a> and by Lemma <a href="/tag/01TH" data-tag="01TH">29.21.6</a> (3) we conclude that $f$ is quasi-finite at $x$. 
    <p>
      Second proof. The fibre $X_ s$ is a scheme locally of finite type over a field, hence locally Noetherian (Lemma <a href="/tag/01T6" data-tag="01T6">29.15.6</a>). The result now follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/01TH" data-tag="01TH">29.21.6</a> and Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0H7C" data-tag="0H7C">28.10.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>